WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.212
- Three years ago, I almost became famous

00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:06.067
in a small Mediterranean
country, and this is that story.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.317
It all started in 2014, when the world

00:00:08.317 --> 00:00:10.716
was a simpler, better place.

00:00:10.716 --> 00:00:12.641
Like, fidget spinners weren't a thing yet.

00:00:12.641 --> 00:00:15.378
I was working here at Buzzfeed,
writing posts for the site.

00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:17.388
Basically at Buzzfeed we
don't have assignments,

00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:19.135
so it's up to us every single day

00:00:19.135 --> 00:00:20.936
to think about what we're gonna write.

00:00:20.936 --> 00:00:22.533
That's usually a really great thing.

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:24.193
I mean, that's so much freedom.

00:00:24.193 --> 00:00:26.750
But there are days where
you come in and you're like,

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.667
"Uh, I've got nothing, I'm dried up."

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.922
(western music)

00:00:31.922 --> 00:00:36.069
So that's what was happening
on June 18th, 2014.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.885
I had no good ideas.

00:00:37.885 --> 00:00:40.604
As the hours went on, I
started getting nervous,

00:00:40.604 --> 00:00:42.729
that I was wasting an entire workday.

00:00:42.729 --> 00:00:44.352
So I went into overdrive.

00:00:44.352 --> 00:00:45.453
"Think, Erin, think!"

00:00:45.453 --> 00:00:46.548
What did you have for breakfast?

00:00:46.548 --> 00:00:47.687
Oatmeal.

00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:52.593
Okay, 21 things that are
thicker than a bowl of oatmeal?

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:54.029
That's horrible.

00:00:54.029 --> 00:00:56.488
Who eats oatmeal?

00:00:56.488 --> 00:00:57.760
Old people.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.713
What about 34 old people you
have to see before you die?

00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:03.546
Wait, what?

00:01:03.546 --> 00:01:04.379
That's worse.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:06.239
Who's like an old person I know?

00:01:06.239 --> 00:01:07.652
Oh yeah, my grandparents.

00:01:07.652 --> 00:01:09.243
What can I write about my grandparents?

00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:12.057
I know that they were all
born here, except for one.

00:01:12.057 --> 00:01:13.892
My grandfather was born in Malta.

00:01:13.892 --> 00:01:16.732
And to be honest, I didn't
really know what Malta was.

00:01:16.732 --> 00:01:18.161
So I Googled it.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:21.747
I hit search, I hit images,
and bam, there it was.

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:22.952
Malta.

00:01:22.952 --> 00:01:26.624
Holy shit, this place is beautiful.

00:01:26.624 --> 00:01:28.799
I don't know why I always
assumed it would look

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:30.813
dreary and gray like most of Europe.

00:01:30.813 --> 00:01:32.628
It couldn't have been more opposite.

00:01:32.628 --> 00:01:35.263
I mean, this place looked
like an iPhone background.

00:01:35.263 --> 00:01:37.247
Everything is bright and colorful,

00:01:37.247 --> 00:01:39.297
the doors are red, and green, and blue.

00:01:39.297 --> 00:01:41.164
And the boats in the
harbor are the same colors,

00:01:41.164 --> 00:01:44.635
and it's just like, why did my
family ever leave this place?

00:01:44.635 --> 00:01:47.142
Well, I just figured out what
I was writing for the day.

00:01:47.142 --> 00:01:50.881
So I picked out the most
beautiful vacation porny

00:01:50.881 --> 00:01:54.825
photos I could find, and I
compiled them into a post.

00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:57.642
I figured it was my duty to let the world,

00:01:57.642 --> 00:01:59.880
or at least like America know,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.073
that Malta is like a real place.

00:02:02.073 --> 00:02:03.611
And you can go there.

00:02:03.611 --> 00:02:05.745
That night, I go home, go to sleep.

00:02:05.745 --> 00:02:07.807
You know, not even thinking
about this post anymore,

00:02:07.807 --> 00:02:09.091
it's totally behind me.

00:02:09.091 --> 00:02:13.757
And then I wake up to a
Biblical flood of notifications.

00:02:13.757 --> 00:02:15.389
(intense music)

00:02:15.389 --> 00:02:18.140
I'm talking Facebook,
I'm talking Instagram,

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.073
I'm talking Twitter.

00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:19.940
Everywhere.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.149
Apparently Malta doesn't
get written about a lot,

00:02:22.149 --> 00:02:24.540
especially by American media sites.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.115
They were pumped.

00:02:27.115 --> 00:02:29.611
I mean like, super super pumped.

00:02:29.611 --> 00:02:30.624
(cheers)

00:02:30.624 --> 00:02:32.262
The people of Malta were messaging me,

00:02:32.262 --> 00:02:35.064
to thank me for the promotion.

00:02:35.064 --> 00:02:36.454
But I was like, "What?

00:02:36.454 --> 00:02:39.878
Thank you for having
such a gorgeous country."

00:02:39.878 --> 00:02:41.287
All this attention reached a point

00:02:41.287 --> 00:02:44.562
where somebody started a gofundme page.

00:02:44.562 --> 00:02:48.246
The page was called, Get Erin 2 Malta,

00:02:48.246 --> 00:02:49.560
(The Buzzfeed Girl).

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.509
And to my sheer horror,

00:02:51.509 --> 00:02:54.477
the page already had several
hundred dollars in it.

00:02:54.477 --> 00:02:56.455
I mean, what is happening?

00:02:56.455 --> 00:02:59.504
I had restaurants and
hotels reaching out saying,

00:02:59.504 --> 00:03:01.070
"Stay with us, it's free!"

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.748
Or, "Eat at my restaurant,
it's on the house."

00:03:03.748 --> 00:03:05.981
This was all super super nice,

00:03:05.981 --> 00:03:07.747
but I didn't expect any of it.

00:03:07.747 --> 00:03:09.996
I mean, I was just trying to write a post.

00:03:09.996 --> 00:03:13.600
As flattered as I was,
I decided I would just

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.960
fade into the background
and let it all die down.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.544
But, of course, it wasn't that easy.

00:03:19.544 --> 00:03:21.912
The next day, somebody sends me a photo.

00:03:21.912 --> 00:03:26.648
It's a picture of the
National newspaper in Malta,

00:03:26.648 --> 00:03:29.133
and in it is my fucking face.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:33.300
This is me in a newspaper on
the other side of the world.

00:03:34.169 --> 00:03:37.311
Headline reads, "Campaign to Thank Woman

00:03:37.311 --> 00:03:39.929
for Extolling Virtues of Malta."

00:03:39.929 --> 00:03:43.152
This had officially become a big deal.

00:03:43.152 --> 00:03:45.264
There was so much attention
surrounding all of this,

00:03:45.264 --> 00:03:46.960
but not all of it was good.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.807
The day after the newspaper,
was another newspaper,

00:03:50.807 --> 00:03:54.078
only this time the writer was not stoked.

00:03:54.078 --> 00:03:55.517
It was really mean.

00:03:55.517 --> 00:03:57.267
The article was basically saying,

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.679
"Who is this Buzzfeed writer,
and why does she think

00:03:59.679 --> 00:04:01.679
she can half-ass some post about Malta

00:04:01.679 --> 00:04:03.365
and get a free trip here?"

00:04:03.365 --> 00:04:05.152
First of all, ouch.

00:04:05.152 --> 00:04:07.487
After that, I pretty much just wanted

00:04:07.487 --> 00:04:09.434
to melt into the floor boards.

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:11.053
I stayed off the internet for a few days

00:04:11.053 --> 00:04:12.653
while the talking heads of Malta

00:04:12.653 --> 00:04:16.310
debated whether I
deserved a dream vacation,

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.669
or to be buried at sea.

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:19.199
(thunder)

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:20.711
As is the way of the internet,

00:04:20.711 --> 00:04:22.247
eventually this did blow over.

00:04:22.247 --> 00:04:26.102
And the Malta thing just became
a story I tell at parties.

00:04:26.102 --> 00:04:29.238
Cut to the year of our Lord, 2017.

00:04:29.238 --> 00:04:30.910
(ominous music)

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.799
My boyfriend and I decide
to take a trip to Italy.

00:04:33.799 --> 00:04:35.900
As we're planning the trip, I noticed,

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.991
we're not gonna be too far

00:04:36.991 --> 00:04:40.064
from a little country called Malta.

00:04:40.064 --> 00:04:42.350
I figured, you know,
enough time has passed,

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.281
people definitely don't remember who I am.

00:04:44.281 --> 00:04:47.158
I check plane tickets from Italy to Malta,

00:04:47.158 --> 00:04:49.574
and they're $35 one way.

00:04:49.574 --> 00:04:53.484
I've literally spent $35 at
McDonald's, so we booked them.

00:04:53.484 --> 00:04:56.570
Next thing I know, I'm on
a fucking plane to Malta.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:57.403
Malta.

00:04:57.403 --> 00:04:59.003
And I'm honestly pretty nervous.

00:04:59.003 --> 00:05:01.113
Was this gonna live up to the hype?

00:05:01.113 --> 00:05:02.714
Dear viewer, it did.

00:05:02.714 --> 00:05:05.795
This place is even more
gorgeous in person.

00:05:05.795 --> 00:05:08.293
And besides that, the
people are incredibly nice,

00:05:08.293 --> 00:05:09.988
the food is incredible.

00:05:09.988 --> 00:05:10.979
It's perfect.

00:05:10.979 --> 00:05:13.896
But I kind of felt like
I had come all this way,

00:05:13.896 --> 00:05:16.502
and it seemed weird to
not at least acknowledge

00:05:16.502 --> 00:05:18.049
everything that had happened.

00:05:18.049 --> 00:05:20.579
So I decided to track down the guy

00:05:20.579 --> 00:05:22.576
who had started that gofundme page.

00:05:22.576 --> 00:05:26.568
I wanted to, I don't know,
thank him, or buy him lunch.

00:05:26.568 --> 00:05:29.989
Or start a campaign to get him to America?

00:05:29.989 --> 00:05:31.387
I don't know what I was doing.

00:05:31.387 --> 00:05:32.390
We decide to grab lunch.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.851
He takes us to this little Maltese deli.

00:05:34.851 --> 00:05:37.695
We're hanging, and I'm
thanking the guy, Chris,

00:05:37.695 --> 00:05:39.100
for being so kind.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.123
Suddenly he puts his
batera down, looks at me,

00:05:42.123 --> 00:05:45.473
and he says, "Did you
ever Google my name?"

00:05:45.473 --> 00:05:47.444
I stopped chewing, and I'm like,

00:05:47.444 --> 00:05:50.334
"No, was I supposed to Google your name?"

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:52.725
He says, "So, you don't know who I am?"

00:05:52.725 --> 00:05:55.695
I say, "I hope not a murderer?"

00:05:55.695 --> 00:05:58.751
Then he asks, "Do you have
20 minutes after lunch?"

00:05:58.751 --> 00:06:01.006
And I tell him, "Yeah, I'm totally free,

00:06:01.006 --> 00:06:02.201
I honestly don't know what

00:06:02.201 --> 00:06:03.720
I'm doing here in the first place."

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.314
So I have zero idea
what's about to happen.

00:06:06.314 --> 00:06:09.110
We walk from the deli to this plaza,

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:11.962
and there's this big, stately building,

00:06:11.962 --> 00:06:13.571
that I'd actually walked past before,

00:06:13.571 --> 00:06:15.011
but had never thought about.

00:06:15.011 --> 00:06:16.918
Chris turns to us and he says,

00:06:16.918 --> 00:06:18.677
"This is the office of
the prime minister."

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:19.633
Oh, cool.

00:06:19.633 --> 00:06:22.530
Okay, maybe he's gonna
take us on a walking tour.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:25.625
But then Chris says,
"We're gonna go inside."

00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:28.041
Before we can even ask what's happening,

00:06:28.041 --> 00:06:31.485
Chris says to us, "This was
my great uncle's office."

00:06:31.485 --> 00:06:33.552
I'm starting to put two and two together,

00:06:33.552 --> 00:06:36.227
and he says, "He was the
prime minister of Malta."

00:06:36.227 --> 00:06:39.389
Okay, cool, we just had
lunch with this dude,

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:43.266
who's great uncle was the
supreme ruler of all of Malta.

00:06:43.266 --> 00:06:45.831
And now we're going into
this fancy-ass building

00:06:45.831 --> 00:06:47.217
dressed like lunatics.

00:06:47.217 --> 00:06:49.753
We walk up the steps, which have cannons

00:06:49.753 --> 00:06:51.825
pointing at us from
either side, by the way.

00:06:51.825 --> 00:06:54.528
This is the Maltese
equivalent of the White House,

00:06:54.528 --> 00:06:56.417
and we're just waltzing in.

00:06:56.417 --> 00:06:58.517
Inside, it's exactly what you think.

00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:00.997
Vaulted ceilings, suits of armor.

00:07:00.997 --> 00:07:02.155
My boyfriend and I are doing that thing

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:04.205
where we're just giggling and saying,

00:07:04.205 --> 00:07:05.864
"What the fuck?" a lot.

00:07:05.864 --> 00:07:07.888
Holy shit, has like Obama been here?

00:07:07.888 --> 00:07:09.932
Actually no, Obama's never been here.

00:07:09.932 --> 00:07:12.111
Wait, Obama's never been
here, and I've been here?

00:07:12.111 --> 00:07:14.359
That's like somehow even cooler to me.

00:07:14.359 --> 00:07:17.253
20 minutes ago I'm eating tuna in a deli,

00:07:17.253 --> 00:07:19.130
and now here I am standing,

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.642
looking at the highest
desk in all of Malta.

00:07:21.642 --> 00:07:23.272
The last thing they
showed us was the roof,

00:07:23.272 --> 00:07:26.074
which had the most incredible view

00:07:26.074 --> 00:07:28.193
of the entire city of Valletta.

00:07:28.193 --> 00:07:31.848
And we're standing up
there, talking, laughing,

00:07:31.848 --> 00:07:34.724
basking in the sun, and it hits me.

00:07:34.724 --> 00:07:39.343
The only reason I'm on top of
the prime minister's office,

00:07:39.343 --> 00:07:42.086
in the country where
my grandfather's from,

00:07:42.086 --> 00:07:44.943
looking out on this gorgeous country,

00:07:44.943 --> 00:07:46.886
is all because I didn't know

00:07:46.886 --> 00:07:49.553
what to write for work one day.

